{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788182866,"nonce":"7LaL+fwKRII0S+1fDbj7zpXj08s=","message":"VERIFIED ON THE LINUX BOX, 2026-08-31 — 130 of 148 checks pass, ZERO red errors.\nStill state:next: two acceptance bullets are not demonstrated and one REAL\nDEFECT was found. Do not close.\n\nDriver: the .ps1 could not run here (no pwsh on this box, none in the Arch\nrepos), so `accept/3.4-pawn-orders.py` was written — same check ids, same raw\nfile protocol, no rwa dependency. Both drivers now exist because BORGES has no\npython and this box has no pwsh; each is the only one that runs where it lives.\n\nBuilt and verified on main MERGED INTO the branch, not the branch alone: 3.4\nsat 16 commits behind, so a branch-only DLL contains no 3.2 code and would be\nan artifact that never ships. Merge was clean; combined Release build is 0\nwarnings / 0 errors, which settles the flagged merge debt as a dedupe question\nrather than a collision (316928 -\u003e 437760 bytes, real IL).\n\nBULLET RESULTS\n\n- Bullet 1 (draft + move + undraft, drafted pawn HOLDS): FULLY PASSED. Every\n  check 1.1-1.11 green, including the 4000-tick hold and the whole-roster\n  `undraft {pawns:\"colonists\"}` form.\n- Bullet 2 (`prioritize haul` hauls it NEXT): NOT DEMONSTRATED — orchestrator\n  staging error, not a verb fault. I sited the fixture stockpile 8x8 where the\n  colonists idle; phase 2 spawns the steel at `pawn:A`, so it landed at\n  [132,131] INSIDE the zone and was already stored. `orders` correctly offered\n  no HaulGeneral. Re-run with the stockpile sited away from the pawns.\n- Bullet 3 (policy-driven re-dress): HALF DEMONSTRATED. 3.6c passed — the\n  disallowed apparel WAS removed, so the filter did drive\n  JobGiver_OptimizeApparel's RemoveApparel pass. But the pawn never wore the\n  parka within 20000 ticks: read after the run it is NAKED and SLEEPING. The\n  wear half needs a free think tick and the rest need took priority. The\n  worker's correction to the spec stands (dev:weather cannot drive this;\n  neededWarmth is the tile's SEASONAL average) — the filter mechanism is right,\n  the advance window is not.\n- Bullet 4 (surgery bill performed by a doctor under advance): FULLY PASSED,\n  inside the FIRST 6000-tick window with no fallback. Anesthetize addable with\n  no missing ingredients, bill visible through 2.4's `bills` observer, bill\n  gone after the advance, and the `Anesthetic` hediff present on the patient.\n\nREAL DEFECT — `warden` applies its levers in the wrong order (5.16b)\n\n`warden {pawns:[p], mode:\"AttemptRecruit\", recruitable:true}` returns ok:true\nwith `applied: [\"recruitable\"]` and\n`refused: [{lever:\"mode\", reason:\"the tab hides this mode for an unrecruitable\nprisoner (hideIfNotRecruitable)\"}]`.\n\nThe mode gate is evaluated against the BEFORE state and `recruitable` is applied\nafterwards, so passing both levers in one call — which 3.4's OWN acceptance\ndoes — silently fails to set the mode. `after.interaction` stays MaintainOnly.\nFix: apply `recruitable` before evaluating the ModeHidden gate, or re-evaluate\nthe gate after the lever pass. The refusal is at least honest and visible,\nwhich is why this is a defect and not a trap.\n\nSPEC GAP — 4.7, 5.1 and 5.2 cannot be driven on a fresh colony\n\n`work-priorities` refuses priority 1 or 2 with, verbatim: \"priority 2 is\nmeaningless with manual priorities off: the Work tab is a checkbox then and\nGetPriority returns a flat 3. Use 0 or 3, or turn manual priorities on in the\nplay settings.\" That refusal is CORRECT and is the gate-in-the-widget doctrine\nworking. But manual priorities default OFF on a new colony and NOTHING in the\n~80-verb surface can turn them on — it is `playSettings.useWorkPriorities`. So\n8 of the 18 failures are unreachable state, not wrong behaviour. Filed\nseparately; 3.4 owes either a lever for it or an acceptance that does not\nassume it.\n\nFAILURE BREAKDOWN (18)\n- 7 orchestrator fixture: 0.1c (game unpaused at start) + 2.3b/2.4a/2.4c/2.4d/\n  2.4e/2.5b (the stockpile siting above)\n- 8 the manual-priorities gap: 4.7a-e, 5.1a-c\n- 2 timing: 3.6a, 3.6b (the sleeping pawn)\n- 1 real defect: 5.16b (warden lever ordering)\n\nEVIDENCE ALSO WORTH KEEPING\n\n- Zero red errors across BOTH runs, including a first run against a colony in a\n  death spiral where 4 of 5 colonists were downed and the surgery patient DIED\n  mid-run. Every verb refused cleanly: `undraft` on the whole roster returned\n  gates [\"downed\",\"downed\",\"downed\",\"downed\",\"downed\",\"already\"], and `assign`\n  on the dead pawn returned a clean bad-args naming the id. That run proved the\n  gates under adversity even though it proved nothing about the bullets.\n- All 35 ops registered live (0.2 green).\n- The guarded routes reported `source:\"backing-field\"` at 3.4d, 4.4b and 5.9d.\n- 5.15b's bad-args names the red error it prevents; 5.12c confirms a refused\n  verb journals NOTHING.\n\nNEW HAZARD INSTANCE, recorded for DESIGN: `Dialog_NamePlayerFactionAndSettlement`\nforce-paused the game mid-run on the first fixture and `advance` returned\nreason:\"dialog\". A naming dialog on the ordinary play path is a 1.7-class wedge\nnot previously in the list, and is concrete evidence for 3.5 being M1-critical.\n\nFixture now saved as the bench's `autostart.rws` (quicktest map, 3 healthy\ncolonists, research bench, 32 startable projects, Anesthetize addable). It needs\nthe stockpile re-sited before the next run.","files":null}]}